cond form''s pools take S.D.C. and hit points only), the S.D.C.-world 1D4x100+25 S.D.C. and A.R. 12, flight and its speed, the in-flight bonuses (conditional), the tail''s own strike, parry and dodge bonus and its penalties (they apply to tail attacks only), claws, power punch and bite, and the +2 Horror Factor if mistaken for a real dragon. || SKILLS: base is the catalog base plus the printed bonus. Dragonese is a named row at 95, per_level 0. The native tongue is a pick from Language: Other at +45 (95%). Hunt is Hunting; Track Animals is Track & Trap Animals; Athletics: General is Athletics (general). W.P. Staff or Blunt is a pick of one; W.P. of choice is any W.P. || HAND TO HAND: Basic granted; Expert costs one related pick, Martial Arts two, Assassin two and only if evil. || RELATED (shared with the Monster Were-Dragon, row 57): eight at level one with floors of two Physical and two Wilderness, and one at levels 2, 5, 8, 11 and 14. Communications is Radio: Basic only (+5%); Domestic +10%; Espionage is Intelligence only; Medical is Paramedic or Holistic Medicine (+5%); Military is Camouflage (+5%); Physical except Gymnastics; Pilot is Hover Craft (ground), Hovercycles, Skycycles & Rocket Bikes, Boat: Sail Type, Boat: Motor, Race & Hydrofoil and Automobile only; the Pilot line''s Horsemanship (general +5%) is the Horsemanship category''s Horsemanship: General at +5%; Pilot Related any; Rogue except Computer Hacking, the selfish-or-evil condition a restriction line; Science -5% as a category bonus; Technical except Computer Programming, its +5% to languages and lore only is a restriction line and not a category bonus; Weapon Proficiencies except W.P. Heavy M.D. Weapons and W.P. Heavy Military Weapons (normal Were-Dragons cannot select Heavy Weapons of any kind); Wilderness +5%. Cowboy, Electrical and Mechanical are none and not listed. Secondary: four at level one and one at levels 3, 6, 9, 12 and 15 from the same list without the bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: catalog rows by slug. The loincloth or loose garb is clothing. The staff or blunt weapon is a pick of quarterstaff or mace; the light energy weapon a pick of two common laser pistols, the book naming none. || MONEY: player characters 3D4x100 credits; slaves none, a restriction line. || NOT STORED: size, weight, life span, habitat, slave market value (100,000 to 400,000 credits), allies and enemies are in the body. The Monster Were-Dragon''s M.D.C., P.P.E., skills, penalties and craving table are not in this class."
